stateDiagram-v2
    %% CURRENT implementation; sources and guards in transition inventory.
    state "OTP expired/cleared (derived)" as inactive
    state "otp_active? true (derived)" as active
    state "locked? true (derived)" as locked
    [*] --> inactive
    inactive --> active: store_otp
    active --> active: store_otp reissue
    active --> locked: increment_attempts! threshold
    locked --> active: lockout clock elapsed
    active --> inactive: OTP deadline elapsed / clear_otp
    locked --> inactive: clear_otp reset_attempts true
    note right of inactive
        The channel policy is independent of the other channel.
        Issuance and window expiry preserve failure counts.
        Issuance timing uses otp_last_sent_at, never created_at.
        Labels are overlapping predicates, not an enum.
        store_otp preserves an active lock.
        clear_otp(false) can leave a locked expired OTP.
        Signup issuance and verification require the candidate owner
        to match the locked Ticket principal, rechecked under the contact lock.
        Released binding facts refuse signup issuance and verification without OTP mutation.
        Admissible signup verification also checks the EmailOtpVerificationFailureBudget destination counter.
        Recreated candidates, flows and browsers cannot reset that separate budget.
        Sign-in resend state binds Auth continuity and immutable Contact/owner facts.
        Released Contacts refuse rotation; dummy state cannot adopt a later binding.
        Accepted email receipt, valid-state resend and well-formed verification
        use a shared 100ms response floor; OTP and budget deadlines are unchanged.
    end note
